M135 GATE BATTERY — label m135b
==============================

Machine: Windows 10 (10.0.19045), 2026-09-25 evening
Build:   CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1, CARGO_TARGET_DIR outside the repo
Why an external target dir: Avira had pinned the in-repo artifact path
  target/debug/deps/epsilon_tools-<hash>.exe, so every test that created a file
  failed with "Access is denied (os error 5)" while every test that did not
  passed. A byte-identical COPY of the same binary run from %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp
  passed, which is what identified the cause as the path and not the code.
  See agents/memory/next-hardening.md.

Why this is label m135b and not m135a: battery m135a was started earlier on an
older byte state, was still running when the review's source fixes landed, and
was then killed mid-test-leg by the harness. It reached 13 of 49 test binaries
and never printed GATE PASS, so per AGENTS.md it proves nothing. This battery
was run in the foreground against the final bytes, after the review fixes and
after the negative control was re-run and files.rs was restored byte-identically.

